---
import {
  Database01Icon,
  Key01Icon,
  SearchList01Icon,
} from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons'
import FeaturePage from '@/components/FeaturePage.astro'

const related = [
  { title: 'seo research', text: 'Every research action, its inputs and how to run it.', href: '/docs/research', icon: SearchList01Icon },
  { title: 'API keys', text: 'Add a DataForSEO or Ahrefs key to the hosted MCP or the CLI.', href: '/docs/keys', icon: Key01Icon },
  { title: 'seo data', text: 'The queries your site already gets, from Search Console.', href: '/docs/data', icon: Database01Icon },
]
---

<FeaturePage
  title="SEO keyword research tool for AI agents"
  description="Run keyword research from your AI agent with your own DataForSEO or Ahrefs key: keyword metrics, SERPs, ranked keywords, competitors and backlinks."
  path="/features/keyword-research"
  lead="Ask your agent for search volume, who ranks, and what a competitor ranks for, with data from your own DataForSEO or Ahrefs account."
  {related}
>
  <h2>Research with the account you already pay for</h2>
  <p>
    Keyword research uses your own DataForSEO or Ahrefs key, so the provider
    bills you directly and nothing is marked up. Add the key on the hosted MCP
    sign-in page, as a header, or with <code>seo providers dataforseo connect</code>
    in the CLI. Keys are never stored on the hosted server.
  </p>

  <h2>What you can look up</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Action</th><th>What comes back</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>keyword_metrics</code></td><td>Search volume, keyword difficulty and cost per click for up to 100 keywords.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>serp</code></td><td>The pages that rank for up to 5 keywords.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>ranked_keywords</code></td><td>The keywords a domain or URL ranks for.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>competitors</code></td><td>Domains that rank for the same keywords.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>backlinks</code></td><td>Referring domains for a domain or URL.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Rows with a domain also get a free Domain Rating column, with no key
    needed. It is Domain Rating by <a href="https://ahrefs.com" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Ahrefs</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Start from the queries you already get</h2>
  <p>
    Provider numbers are estimates. Your Search Console queries are what
    people actually typed before they found you. Ask for those first with
    <a href="/docs/data">seo data</a> or the <a href="/docs/report">SEO report</a>,
    then use research to size the topics around them. The two sources stay
    apart and are never mixed into one number.
  </p>
</FeaturePage>
